        "number": 19512,
        "title": "Record the time consuming of memory operation of Insert Executor in Runtime Information",
        "body": "## Description\r\n## Development Task\r\n\r\nINSERT IGNORE from a table of 300,000 rows,\r\n\r\n```mysql\r\nINSERT IGNORE INTO t SELECT * FROM t1\r\n```\r\nAnd we got the following slow query log.\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/867381/91382035-6016db00-e85b-11ea-8935-23d6fb85e915.png)\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, with this log, we have no clue where the time is consumed. \r\n\r\nThen we must investigate this problem by using go profile or trace.\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/867381/91382564-96088f00-e85c-11ea-9850-dfea23c81a3d.png)\r\n\r\nWith the above go profile graph, I propose to add two extra time-consuming sections in runtime information and trace span,\r\n1. Check Duplicate, including [`getKeysNeedCheck`](https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/650be7c4383a197a0311433572d082eb087217a2/executor/insert_common.go#L952) and [`txn.Get` from memory buffer](https://github.com/pingcap/tidb/blob/650be7c4383a197a0311433572d082eb087217a2/executor/insert_common.go#L978), but except the RPC time.\r\n2. Add Records, for the memory operation of memtable.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n## SIG slack channel\r\n[#sig-exec](https://slack.tidb.io/invite?team=tidb-community&channel=sig-exec&ref=high-performance)\r\n\r\n## Score\r\n- 300\r\n\r\n## Mentor\r\n * @qw4990 \r\n",
        "comments": [
            "/label sig/execution",
            "@jyz0309 PTAL",
            "/pick-up",
            "Pick up success."
        ]
    },
